IN THE SUPREME COURT OF INDIA
CASE NO: Civil Appeal No. 6239 of 2019
CITATION: (2019) 5 SCC 725
YEAR: 2019

CORAM / BENCH:
Hon'ble Judges: U.U. Lalit, Indu Malhotra

PARTIES:
Pioneer Urban Land vs Govindan Raghavan

STATUTES & ACTS REFERRED:
Consumer Protection Act, 1986, Indian Contract Act, 1872

KEY PROVISIONS & SECTIONS:
Section 2(1)(g) Consumer Protection, Section 23 Contract Act

LEGAL KEYWORDS & TOPICS:
one-sided builder contract, unfair trade practice, homebuyer delay refund

================================================================================
                    JUDGMENT SUMMARY & RATIO DECIDENDI
================================================================================

Held that builder-buyer agreements containing one-sided and unfair conditions cannot be enforced against homebuyers, constituting an unfair trade practice.

1. ISSUES CONSIDERED:
   The court addressed questions of legal interpretation under Section 2(1)(g) Consumer Protection, Section 23 Contract Act.

2. ANALYSIS & PRECEDENT CONTEXT:
   Having examined the statutory scheme, fundamental principles of jurisprudence,
   and constitutional safeguards, the Court reiterated the necessity of strict
   compliance with statutory procedure and evidentiary standards.

3. HELD & BINDING RATIO:
   The principle formulated in this judgment constitutes binding judicial precedent
   within its territorial and appellate jurisdiction.

